From 743531aea9ed287f0c64a77ac683f30fd43fd307 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:03:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rdnshc, www: LAN name resolution check - amber Internet
 state, tooltip, DNS Failover switch

The dashboard said "Connected" whenever the WAN held an address, so a box
whose LAN devices could not resolve a single name still read green.
rc/rdnshc.c now asks the path LAN devices use once a minute (the first
check 15 s after start) whether or not the health check is on: the
router's DNS for "localhost" on lan_ipaddr:53 and for a random label under
reaper_landns_domain (dns_probe_host, then a fixed name, when the setting
is empty or invalid), or the servers DHCP hands out when the admin set
any; held while the primary WAN is down; two bad checks in a row turn it
bad, one good one clears; a failing fresh name asks each upstream directly
to name the silent ones. Published as nvram reaper_landns_state
"<state> <s> <silent|->", cleared when the daemon stops; one syslog line
when it turns bad, one when it recovers. Status only: the DNS list,
dnsmasq and link_internet are never touched. dns_ask() is probe_addr()'s
core, lifted out (same verdict).

defaults.c: reaper_landns_enable=1 (a missing key = on), reaper_landns_domain
empty. Main_ReaperDash.asp: the WAN pill and the Internet card keep the word
"Connected"; the dot and the word turn amber while the check fails, and one
page-level tooltip on both explains the state (text nodes only; hover for a
mouse, focus or tap opens, a click pins, Esc / elsewhere / scroll / resize
close; none in AP / repeater / bridge mode). Reaper_Failover.asp: the switch,
the domain (validated as the daemon does) and the live state, posted with
restart_rdnshc. 25 language packs: RDSH_91-103, RDHC_59-64, and RFW_328 for
the list-save pre-check of the next commit (the packs move in lockstep).
Lean: tests/test_landns_check.py.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
